<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Cayman</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grand Cayman is the largest of the three Cayman Islands in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, and holds most of the territory's population. Permanent settlement began in the 18th century with settlers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> and the enslaved Africans they brought. Its capital, George Town, and its beaches make it the centre of the islands' finance and tourism economies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grand-cayman.jpg" alt="Grand Cayman" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_cayman.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
